./expeditions/2026-06-20-aoyagi-full/synthesis.md:419:Pen-and-paper af574d00 (`tobl3b-routeB-reversal-cert.md`, decorrelated-Codex-concurred + Codex independently proved the structure): **Route B REFUTED.** The "≥1 divergence-free end" claim is FALSE — min counterexample **(2,1,2)** (palindromic 3-width waist, head-split divergent from BOTH ends; reversal = no 2nd orientation). ★ **The real boundary is the PIVOT criterion `u·ρ≥minAdm(redChain u M)` (ρ=min tail width) — the genuine head-split ROUTE wall (C_hle §5, exact map rank `=u·ρ`), STRICTLY STRONGER than the corank criterion (pivot⊋corank; corank-only=0, pivot-only=6844).** This REVERSES the a2ee13b4 route-B hope (its 0/764 was under the WEAKER corank criterion). **The co-minimizer does NOT rescue the pivot** (0/35; the waist forces the pivot rank `u` small) — so unlike the corank divergence (a bound artifact), the pivot wall is a genuine limitation OF THE HEAD-SPLIT ROUTE (though the TRUE integral is still finite, Watanabe+Aoyagi). **Clean structural theorem (Codex-proved, exhaustive-verified):** two-ended obstruction occurs ONLY for 3-width strict-waist triples `y<min(x,z)`; ≥4-width front-fail forces M₁<M_{L-1}, back-fail M_{L-1}<M₁ (impossible) — BUT a good top end does NOT save route B (1506 ≥4-width chains descend into an irreducible waist; 8653 not transitively dischargeable). Reversal CoV `I(M)=I(reverse M)` SOUND + Lean-adjacent (transposition+factor-reversal, |det|=1; combinatorial half banked via `minAdm_comp_perm∘Fin.rev`; integral half a small new lemma w/ the matrix-measure diamond friction) but INSUFFICIENT (needs a good end; waists lack it). **⟹ Route A (finer Z_deep-stratification) FORCED; the `y<min(x,z)` characterization scopes it to a sharp hard core.** **RECALIBRATION: the T-Obl3b mountain is a TWO-REGIME construction** — (1) non-waist (`u·ρ≥minAdm`): the head-split S1 (de-risked: s1-spine-headsplit + C_hle-finite); (2) waist (`y<min(x,z)`): route A = a DIRECT bottleneck resolution (a2ee13b