MS (a) vs orbit-stabiliser/Chevalley (b) [pen-and-paper, 2026-06-19]\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/21-route-sizing/findings.md:3:## VERDICT: ROUTE (a) smooth-point assembly — smaller by a large factor. KMS determinantal sub-library AVOIDED.\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/21-route-sizing/findings.md:8:  `dim source = dim target + dim fibre` in any form. Orbit-dimension package ABSENT. `ringKrullDim = trdeg` for\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/21-route-sizing/findings.md:9:  f.g. domain/field ABSENT (so even the trdeg-additivity route to (b) is blocked). ⟹ route (b) = a from-scratch\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/21-route-sizing/findings.md:14:- **Determinantal PRIMENESS (KMS/Lakshmibai–Magyar) NOT needed.** Take `I = vanishingIdeal(Z_M)` directly —\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/21-route-sizing/findings.md:15:  prime from `isPrime_vanishingIdeal_orbitSet` (O_M irreducible, LANDED) + `Z_M = Ō_M` (L6). The cotangent/regular\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/21-route-sizing/findings.md:16:  chain runs on the reduced ring; never need \"(minors) = vanishingIdeal\".\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/21-route-sizing/findings.md:18:  (intrinsic). NOT via minor pderivs (that would re-import determinantal primeness — guard K2: use dμ_M=δ⁰).\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/21-route-sizing/findings.md:21:`varietyDim(Z_M) =[L4d] ringKrullDim(AtPrime m_M) =[M3 smooth⟹regular] finrank(cotangent) =[L2a, LANDED]\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/21-route-sizing/findings.md:27:- L6.3 easy direction (rank lower-semicontinuity, Ō_M ⊆ Z_M) ☐ module. L6.4 `vanishingIdeal(Z_M)=vanishingIdeal(O_M)`\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/21-route-sizing/findings.md:28:  ideal-level ☐ module (reuses `vanishingIdeal_range_orbitMap_eq_ker`). L1 `(vanishingIdeal Z_M).IsPrime` ☐ short.\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/21-route-sizing/codex/route-sizing-answer.md:3:1. **No.** Chevalley constructibility exists (`PrimeSpectrum.isConstructible_comap_image`, `Scheme.Hom.isConstructible_image`), and trdeg additivity exists (`Algebra.trdeg` `[stacks 030G]`, `trdeg_add_eq` `[stacks 030H]`), but I found no fibre-dimension theorem / Stacks `02FZ`, `02NM`, `05F6`-usable declaration.\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/21-route-sizing/codex/route-sizing-answer.md:10:   - **(b3) Partial, not enough.** Trdeg and Noether normalization exist (`trdeg_add_eq`, `NoetherNormalization.exists_finite_inj_algHom_of_fg` `[stacks 00OW]`), but I found no `ringKrullDim = trdeg` theorem for finitely generated domains.\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/21-route-sizing/codex/route-sizing-answer.md:12:4. **No.** Matrix minors/rank infrastructure exists (`Matrix.submatrix`, `Matrix.det`, `Matrix.rank`, `Matrix.rank_submatrix_le`), but I found no determinantal-ideal primeness/radical/CM theory, variety-of-complexes, or quiver-locus ideal package.\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/21-route-sizing/codex/route-sizing-answer.md:14:5. **Decision: route (a) is the smaller remaining Lean build, likely by a large factor.** Given your landed smooth/local/Jacobian bedrock, route (a) can avoid full determinantal-ideal primeness if `Z_M = closure O_M` is proved set-theoretically: `O_M` irreducible implies `Z_M` irreducible/prime, and homogeneity plus dense smooth locus gives smoothness of `M`; the genuinely new content is then `Z_M = closure O_M`, smoothness via homogeneity, and `ker Jac_M = range δ⁰`. Route (b) would require building Chevalley fibre dimension plus an algebraic orbit-dimension layer essentially from scratch.\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/21-route-sizing/codex/route-sizing-answer.md:16:Caveat: the Jacobian step must compare the cotangent space of the reduced/prime `Z_M` with the chosen minor equations. That does **not** require global d