y a large factor.** Given your landed smooth/local/Jacobian bedrock, route (a) can avoid full determinantal-ideal primeness if `Z_M = closure O_M` is proved set-theoretically: `O_M` irreducible implies `Z_M` irreducible/prime, and homogeneity plus dense smooth locus gives smoothness of `M`; the genuinely new content is then `Z_M = closure O_M`, smoothness via homogeneity, and `ker Jac_M = range δ⁰`. Route (b) would require building Chevalley fibre dimension plus an algebraic orbit-dimension layer essentially from scratch.\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/21-route-sizing/codex/route-sizing-stdout.log:7076:Caveat: the Jacobian step must compare the cotangent space of the reduced/prime `Z_M` with the chosen minor equations. That does **not** require global determinantal primeness, but it does require either using the vanishing ideal in the bridge or proving the minor generators give the correct first-order equations at `M`.\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/21-route-sizing/codex/route-sizing-stdout.log:7078:6. **Sharpest risk: `Z_M = closure O_M` for equioriented type A.** It balloons if formalized as scheme-theoretic/radical ideal equality or via full Lakshmibai-Magyar/KMS determinantal primeness; keep it as a set-theoretic degeneration-order theorem plus a separate first-order Jacobian lemma.\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/21-route-sizing/codex/route-sizing-prompt.md:15:- The polynomial-ring catenary/dimension formula `height p + ringKrullDim(R/p) = n` for R = k[x_1..x_n].\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/21-route-sizing/codex/route-sizing-prompt.md:16:- An affine-domain dimension formula `height p + ringKrullDim(A/p) = ringKrullDim A` and\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/21-route-sizing/codex/route-sizing-prompt.md:17:  local↔global `ringKrullDim(Localization.AtPrime m) = ringKrullDim A` for a finite-type domain A.\n./expeditions/2026-06-18-voigt-discharge/threads/21-route-sizing/c